From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:11:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Fixes from a review of the whole series

- clear recentblocks for an index with nothing indexed, so hashes left from a
  deleted index cannot hide a reorg at the new tip
- a node behind the index on the same chain (it knows the index's last block
  among its headers) is waited for, not called another chain
- the startup rollback stops at the index's first block
- mempool prevouts through gettxout on any node without txindex, not only a
  pruned one
- headers.subscribe checks the tip it answers with; protocolVersion volatile
- off a v2 chain, server.features reports this server's range, not the
  backend's, and no fork point
- log which chain the node is on (for packagers), and no 'backend configured'
  warning for a blank backend
---
 .../frigate/bitcoind/BitcoindClient.java      | 47 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../electrum/ElectrumServerService.java       | 27 ++++++++++-
 .../frigate/io/RecentBlocksMap.java           |  7 +++
 .../bitcoind/FutureWitnessProgramTest.java    | 29 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

